{"content":[{"c":["GRIEF"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Emotional suffering brought on by bereavement, mishap, or disaster. To grieve is either to cause or feel sorrow or distress. The concept is found in the Scriptures under a variety of circumstances. Isaac and Rebekah experienced grief when their son Esau married a Hittite woman (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.26.35","r":"Gen.26.35","rawR":"Gen.26.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.26.35","value":"Gen.26.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 26:35"},"). God mourned the misery of Israel brought upon them by disobedience (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.10.16","r":"Judg.10.16","rawR":"Judg.10.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.10.16","value":"Judg.10.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 10:16"},"). Because she had no son, Hannah was sad—so much so that she appeared to be drunk while praying (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.1.16","r":"1Sam.1.16","rawR":"1Sam.1.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.1.16","value":"1Sam.1.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 1:16"},"). Similarly, Samuel, distraught at King Saul’s disobedience, prayed all night. Job was exceedingly sorrowful over his personal loss (",{"href":"?bref=Job.2.13","r":"Job.2.13","rawR":"Job.2.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.2.13","value":"Job.2.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 2:13"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Job.6.2","r":"Job.6.2","rawR":"Job.6.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.6.2","value":"Job.6.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.16.6","r":"Job.16.6","rawR":"Job.16.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.16.6","value":"Job.16.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:6"},"), and the psalmist poetically demonstrated distress and sorrow (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.6.7","r":"Ps.6.7","rawR":"Ps.6.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.6.7","value":"Ps.6.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 6:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.31.9-10","r":"Ps.31.9-10","rawR":"Ps.31.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.31.9-10","value":"Ps.31.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"31:9-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.69.26","r":"Ps.69.26","rawR":"Ps.69.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.69.26","value":"Ps.69.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"69:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.21","r":"Ps.73.21","rawR":"Ps.73.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.21","value":"Ps.73.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"73:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.95.10","r":"Ps.95.10","rawR":"Ps.95.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.95.10","value":"Ps.95.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"95:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.112.10","r":"Ps.112.10","rawR":"Ps.112.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.112.10","value":"Ps.112.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"112:10"},"). The book of Lamentations is devoted to the expression of grief, and the prophets in general speak of judgment because Israel had grieved a holy God."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Jesus experienced sorrow and distress (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.3.5","r":"Mark.3.5","rawR":"Mark.3.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.3.5","value":"Mark.3.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 3:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.11.33","r":"John.11.33","rawR":"John.11.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.33","value":"John.11.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 11:33"},"), including crying over the death of a friend (",{"href":"?bref=John.11.35","r":"John.11.35","rawR":"John.11.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.35","value":"John.11.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 11:35"},"). The Jews are said to have been grieved as the apostles taught about Christ (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.4.2","r":"Acts.4.2","rawR":"Acts.4.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.4.2","value":"Acts.4.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 4:2"},"). The apostle Paul instructed believers not to grieve one another (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.14.15","r":"Rom.14.15","rawR":"Rom.14.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.14.15","value":"Rom.14.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 14:15"},") and did not want to cause any sorrow himself (",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.2.1-5","r":"2Cor.2.1-5","rawR":"2Cor.2.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.2.1-5","value":"2Cor.2.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Cor 2:1-5"},"). Most of all, the believer is not to grieve the Holy Spirit (",{"href":"?bref=Eph.4.30","r":"Eph.4.30","rawR":"Eph.4.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.4.30","value":"Eph.4.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 4:30"},"). A believer may, of course, experience grief and suffering in an alien world (",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.2.19","r":"1Pet.2.19","rawR":"1Pet.2.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.2.19","value":"1Pet.2.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pt 2:19"},"). In Bible times grief was given particular expression at a time of death by means of shrieks, wails, and laments (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.9.17-18","r":"Jer.9.17-18","rawR":"Jer.9.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.9.17-18","value":"Jer.9.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 9:17-18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.5.16","r":"Amos.5.16","rawR":"Amos.5.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.5.16","value":"Amos.5.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 5:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.38","r":"Mark.5.38","rawR":"Mark.5.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.38","value":"Mark.5.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 5:38"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Mourning_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Mourning_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Mourning_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mourning"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Grief","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 26:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.26.35","rawQueryValue":"Gen.26.35","sourceRefExact":"Gen.26.35"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 10:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.10.16","rawQueryValue":"Judg.10.16","sourceRefExact":"Judg.10.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 1:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.1.16","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.1.16","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.1.16"},{"anchorText":"Jb 2:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.2.13","rawQueryValue":"Job.2.13","sourceRefExact":"Job.2.13"},{"anchorText":"6:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.6.2","rawQueryValue":"Job.6.2","sourceRefExact":"Job.6.2"},{"anchorText":"16:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.16.6","rawQueryValue":"Job.16.6","sourceRefExact":"Job.16.6"},{"anchorText":"Pss 6:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.6.7","rawQueryValue":"Ps.6.7","sourceRefExact":"Ps.6.7"},{"anchorText":"31:9-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.31.9-10","rawQueryValue":"Ps.31.9-10","sourceRefExact":"Ps.31.9-10"},{"anchorText":"69:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.69.26","rawQueryValue":"Ps.69.26","sourceRefExact":"Ps.69.26"},{"anchorText":"73:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.73.21","rawQueryValue":"Ps.73.21","sourceRefExact":"Ps.73.21"},{"anchorText":"95:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.95.10","rawQueryValue":"Ps.95.10","sourceRefExact":"Ps.95.10"},{"anchorText":"112:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.112.10","rawQueryValue":"Ps.112.10","sourceRefExact":"Ps.112.10"},{"anchorText":"Mk 3:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.3.5","rawQueryValue":"Mark.3.5","sourceRefExact":"Mark.3.5"},{"anchorText":"Jn 11:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.11.33","rawQueryValue":"John.11.33","sourceRefExact":"John.11.33"},{"anchorText":"Jn 11:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.11.35","rawQueryValue":"John.11.35","sourceRefExact":"John.11.35"},{"anchorText":"Acts 4:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.4.2","rawQueryValue":"Acts.4.2","sourceRefExact":"Acts.4.2"},{"anchorText":"Rom 14:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.14.15","rawQueryValue":"Rom.14.15","sourceRefExact":"Rom.14.15"},{"anchorText":"2 Cor 2:1-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Cor.2.1-5","rawQueryValue":"2Cor.2.1-5","sourceRefExact":"2Cor.2.1-5"},{"anchorText":"Eph 4:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Eph.4.30","rawQueryValue":"Eph.4.30","sourceRefExact":"Eph.4.30"},{"anchorText":"1 Pt 2:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Pet.2.19","rawQueryValue":"1Pet.2.19","sourceRefExact":"1Pet.2.19"},{"anchorText":"Jer 9:17-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.9.17-18","rawQueryValue":"Jer.9.17-18","sourceRefExact":"Jer.9.17-18"},{"anchorText":"Am 5:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.5.16","rawQueryValue":"Amos.5.16","sourceRefExact":"Amos.5.16"},{"anchorText":"Mk 5:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.5.38","rawQueryValue":"Mark.5.38","sourceRefExact":"Mark.5.38"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"96c89f4de102fbdea8cd99b783ca6c85c1f963760bbf177430d3175f72e77723","sourceItemName":"Grief","sourceItemOrder":215,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Grief","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Grief","title":"Grief","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}